DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss utility verifies and repairs FAT file systems (more com‐
     monly known as DOS file systems).

     The first form of ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss preens the specified file systems.  It is
     normally started by fsck(8) run from _/_e_t_c_/_r_c during automatic reboot,
     when a FAT file system is detected.  When preening file systems,
     ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss will fix common inconsistencies non-interactively.  If more
     serious problems are found, ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss does not try to fix them, indi‐
     cates that it was not successful, and exits.

     The second form of ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss checks the specified file systems and
     tries to repair all detected inconsistencies, requesting confirmation be‐
     fore making any changes.

     The options are as follows:

     --CC      Compatibility with the corresponding fsck(8) option (skip check
             if clean), defined to no-op.

     --FF      Compatibility with the wrapper fsck(8) which seeks to determine
             whether the file system needs to be cleaned immediately in fore‐
             ground, or if its cleaning can be deferred to background.  FAT
             (MS-DOS) file systems must always be cleaned in the foreground.
             A non-zero exit code is always returned for this option.

     --MM      Causes ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss to not use mmap(2) when checking a FAT32 file
             system.  This option is mainly for debugging purposes and is not
             normally necessary.  The ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss utility will automatically
             fall back to use a simple LRU cache of 4 MiB when it failed to
             perform mmap(2), or when --MM is specified.

     --ff      Force ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss to check “clean” file systems when preening.

     --nn      Causes ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss to assume “no” as the answer to all operator
             questions, except “CONTINUE?”.

     --pp      Preen the specified file systems.

     --yy      Causes ffsscckk__mmssddoossffss to assume “yes” as the answer to all operator
             questions.

